l/status/2109232467131404686"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2109204297665970176"],"media_source_tweet_id":["2109204360240742593"]},"author_id":"1179892477714718721","conversation_id":"2109225066823323964","created_at":"2026-10-11T10:10:18.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109225066823323964"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/vpGF36vi9s","end":100,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Nature__77/status/2109204360240742593/video/1","media_key":"13_2109204297665970176","start":77,"url":"https://t.co/vpGF36vi9s"}]},"id":"2109225066823323964","lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":25,"impression_count":29297,"like_count":168,"quote_count":3,"reply_count":17,"retweet_count":17},"text":"Remote physical interaction through technology \n\nHow do you feel about this? https://t.co/vpGF36vi9s","url":"https://x.com/sciencegirl/status/2109225066823323964"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2109220958787502080"]},"author_id":"2311987360","conversation_id":"2109221315769221401","created_at":"2026-10-11T09:55:23.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109221315769221401"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/Tlnj6LaIs7","end":161,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2109221315769221401/video/1","media_key":"13_2109220958787502080","start":138,"url":"https://t.co/Tlnj6LaIs7"},{"display_url":"x.com/marclou/status…","end":185,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/marclou/status/2108958258308534488","start":162,"url":"https://t.co/aZRMfW5PPW"}]},"id":"2109221315769221401","lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":89,"impression_count":25468,"like_count":388,"quote_count":3,"reply_count":80,"retweet_count":12},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2108958258308534488","type":"quoted"}],"text":"I wanted to remap the mouse buttons, so I asked Opus 5.5 to build me a macOS app.\n\nOne prompt. 5 minutes.\n\nWhat a great time to be alive. https://t.co/Tlnj6LaIs7 https://t.co/aZRMfW5PPW","url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2109221315769221401"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109214434526625792"]},"author_id":"1573399256836309009","conversation_id":"2109215182035583229","created_at":"2026-10-11T09:31:01.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109215182035583229"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/Eb9Hxb82Uj","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/kimmonismus/status/2109215182035583229/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109214434526625792","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/Eb9Hxb82Uj"},{"display_url":"x.com/a16z/status/21…","end":327,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/a16z/status/2108663228029112702","start":304,"url":"https://t.co/80rkcugpAN"}]},"id":"2109215182035583229","lang":"en","note_tweet":{"text":"I think this is one of the most important graphs of the last few months, and perhaps years. For a long time, there was speculation about how AI would affect the labor market.\n\nClearly, it was only a matter of time before AI reached the white-collar sector, but empirical evidence was scarce, ultimately because, of course, one only really understands how the market situation develops in retrospect.\n\nNow, as in this example, we see that AI is clearly and unequivocally entering certain professions and replacing people. Call center agents are the first to be replaced. And as more AI and agents enter the workforce, a similar process will spread to other areas of work. Frankly, I don't believe that AI will necessarily create new jobs, resulting in a net zero. I think more jobs will be replaced than created. This needs to be discussed."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":166,"impression_count":28810,"like_count":564,"quote_count":15,"reply_count":71,"retweet_count":38},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2108663228029112702","type":"quoted"}],"text":"I think this is one of the most important graphs of the last few months, and perhaps years. For a long time, there was speculation about how AI would affect the labor market.\n\nClearly, it was only a matter of time before AI reached the white-collar sector, but empirical evidence https://t.co/Eb9Hxb82Uj https://t.co/80rkcugpAN","url":"https://x.com/kimmonismus/status/2109215182035583229"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109209190392573952"]},"author_id":"2311987360","conversation_id":"2109209763158368367","created_at":"2026-10-11T09:09:29.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109209763158368367"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":50,"id":"2676313880","start":42,"username":"Revolut"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/WHyXLfJFLr","end":78,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2109209763158368367/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109209190392573952","start":55,"url":"https://t.co/WHyXLfJFLr"}]},"id":"2109209763158368367","lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":3,"impression_count":12533,"like_count":118,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":44,"retweet_count":0},"text":"My wife just ordered a new credit card on @Revolut \n\n🥹 https://t.co/WHyXLfJFLr","url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2109209763158368367"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109202290728984576"]},"author_id":"1179892477714718721","conversation_id":"2109202295971885321","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:39:49.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109202295971885321"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/EH65JbVOZl","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/sciencegirl/status/2109202295971885321/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109202290728984576","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/EH65JbVOZl"}]},"id":"2109202295971885321","lang":"en","note_tweet":{"text":"Scientists reprogrammed leukemia to switch itself off, and it worked\n\nResearchers at the Institut Pasteur developed a new approach that changes how malignant B-cell leukemia shuts itself down, while also drawing the immune system into action. Most treatments try to remove cancer cells directly, but this method works by triggering a process that sends strong warning signals to immune cells, helping the body recognize and clear the disease. This response normally does not occur in B-cell leukemia because a key molecular component is missing. By combining three clinically used compounds, the researchers were able to work around this limitation and activate the immune response. Using advanced imaging in preclinical models, they observed immune cells rapidly moving in and clearing the leukemia. \n\nIn these experiments, the disease did not just lessen, it was completely cleared. Although this approach has not yet been tested in patients, the findings point to a promising strategy that relies on immune-mediated tumor control, with the potential for faster clinical evaluation because existing compounds were used."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":105,"impression_count":31485,"like_count":532,"quote_count":4,"reply_count":13,"retweet_count":95},"text":"Scientists reprogrammed leukemia to switch itself off, and it worked\n\nResearchers at the Institut Pasteur developed a new approach that changes how malignant B-cell leukemia shuts itself down, while also drawing the immune system into action. Most treatments try to remove cancer https://t.co/EH65JbVOZl","url":"https://x.com/sciencegirl/status/2109202295971885321"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2108930121558380544"],"media_source_tweet_id":["2108930562794864912"]},"author_id":"1573399256836309009","conversation_id":"2109194221773304277","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:07:44.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109194221773304277"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/15Cr2pFcT3","end":279,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/firesidealpha/status/2108930562794864912/video/1","media_key":"13_2108930121558380544","start":256,"url":"https://t.co/15Cr2pFcT3"}]},"id":"2109194221773304277","lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":91,"impression_count":24427,"like_count":584,"quote_count":7,"reply_count":73,"retweet_count":52},"text":"Qualcomm’s CEO says AI companies want smartphones to run 100-billion-parameter models around